@title Route 9 Transit Options
@subtitle Decision page for councillors, vote on 2026-12-02
@author Riverbend City Transportation Department

## Options
cards
### Enhanced bus
- More frequent buses and signal priority at lights
- Capital cost: $85M
- Build time: 2 years
- Weekday riders by 2035: 14,000
- Operating cost: $22M a year

### Bus rapid transit
- Dedicated lanes and stations
- Capital cost: $310M
- Build time: 4 years
- Weekday riders by 2035: 26,000
- Operating cost: $31M a year

### Light rail
- Capital cost: $940M
- Build time: 8 years
- Weekday riders by 2035: 38,000
- Operating cost: $44M a year

## Capital cost per rider
data cpr = option,usd; Enhanced bus,6100; Bus rapid transit,11900; Light rail,24700
chart hbar cpr unit=$ title="Capital cost per weekday rider"

Light rail costs about four times as much per rider as enhanced bus.

## Trade-offs
- Enhanced bus is cheap and fast to deliver. It carries the fewest riders and still shares congested lanes.
- Bus rapid transit is the middle path, and it could be upgraded to rail later.
- Light rail carries the most riders and attracts development. It takes 8 years, and the city could not fund its share without a bond measure.

A federal grant can cover up to 50% of capital cost. The application is due 2027-01-31 and requires a council-approved option.

## Recommendation
The department recommends bus rapid transit.

!! The council must approve an option on 2026-12-02 to meet the federal grant deadline of 2027-01-31.
